mdl 1;
-- Bug ako/mxcli#2145 (mendixlabs/mxcli#1821): the `action:` override of
-- `use building block` only recognised the core buttons (actionbutton,
-- linkbutton, button). A PlatformDesignSystem block is a pluggable PDS Button,
-- so
--   use building block PlatformDesignSystem.Button (action: call microflow PDSRepro.ACT_Noop) as b_
-- failed with
--   Error: failed to build page: use building block PlatformDesignSystem.Button:
--   action override supplied, but the block has no button to rebind
--
-- Fix: with no core button in the block, the override binds the first pluggable
-- widget whose definition has a CLICK action (Source OnClick — PDS Button's
-- onClickAction, Badge Button's onClickEvent, Image's onClick), skipping data
-- containers. A block with a core button binds it as before.
--
-- PlatformDesignSystem is a marketplace module this repo cannot fetch without a
-- marketplace token, so the regression case uses the equivalent Atlas block:
-- Card_WithImage has no core button, only a pluggable Image whose definition
-- declares an onClick action. Verify (project with Atlas_Web_Content, e.g.
-- `mxcli new`): exec writes `image w_image1 (…, OnClick: call microflow
-- BugTest2145.ACT_Noop, …)`; mxcli docker check reports 0 errors.

create module BugTest2145;

create microflow BugTest2145.ACT_Noop () begin end;

create page BugTest2145.Action_Rebind (Title: 'Rebind', Layout: Atlas_Core.Atlas_Default) {
  use building block Atlas_Web_Content.Card_WithImage (action: call microflow BugTest2145.ACT_Noop) as w_
};
